<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Calibration experiment report</title>
<style>
:root{color-scheme:light;--ink:#172f42;--muted:#546778;--paper:#f5f4ef;--line:#cad5dc;--accent:#ad482f}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:var(--paper);color:var(--ink);font:16px/1.55 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:1180px;margin:auto;padding:48px 28px}header{border-bottom:3px solid var(--ink);padding-bottom:28px}h1{font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.3rem);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.04em;margin:10px 0 20px}h2{margin-top:40px}h3{margin:24px 0 12px}.badge{display:inline-block;background:var(--ink);color:white;border-radius:3px;padding:4px 10px;font-size:.8rem;letter-spacing:.08em;text-transform:uppercase}.note{max-width:85ch;color:var(--muted)}.panel{background:white;border:1px solid var(--line);padding:20px;margin:20px 0;overflow:auto}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.86rem}th{text-align:left;color:var(--muted);font-weight:600}td,th{padding:9px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);vertical-align:top}td.num{font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;white-space:nowrap}small{display:block;color:var(--muted);font-size:.65rem}.value{font-weight:650}svg{display:block;margin-top:4px}summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:650}details{margin-top:12px}footer{border-top:1px solid var(--line);margin-top:40px;padding-top:16px;color:var(--muted)}@media(max-width:650px){main{padding:24px 14px}.panel{padding:10px}td,th{padding:7px 6px}}
</style></head><body><main>
{% macro number(item) -%}<span class="value" data-claim="{{ item.id }}">{{ item.value }}</span><small>{{ item.id }}</small>{%- endmacro %}
{% macro validity_table(rows) %}<table><thead><tr><th>Axis / level</th><th>Valid</th><th>Invalid</th><th>Total</th><th>Invalid fraction</th><th>Reasons</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for row in rows %}<tr><td>{{ row.axis }} {{ number(row.level) }}</td><td class="num">{{ number(row.valid) }}</td><td class="num">{{ number(row.invalid) }}</td><td class="num">{{ number(row.total) }}</td><td class="num">{{ number(row.rate) }}{{ row.bar|safe }}</td><td>{% for reason in row.reasons %}{{ reason.text }} {{ number(reason.count) }}{% else %}None{% endfor %}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table>{% endmacro %}
<header><span class="badge">{{ 'Synthetic evidence' if evidence == 'synthetic' else 'Observed evidence' }}</span><h1>Calibration experiment report</h1><p class="note">Metadata corruption changes the assumed calibration while sensor observations stay fixed. Timing stress selects actual available LiDAR and preserves each sensor’s timestamped ego pose. Every displayed measurement is linked to an exact verified scalar claim.</p></header>
{% for context in contexts %}<p data-claim="{{ context.id }}">{{ context.text }}</p>{% endfor %}
{% for item in extras %}<article class="panel" data-claim="{{ item.id }}"><p>{{ item.text }}</p>{{ number(item) }}<small>{{ item.evidence }}</small></article>{% endfor %}
{% for section in sections %}<section><h2>{{ section.method|capitalize }}{% if section.seed %} · seed {{ number(section.seed) }}{% endif %}</h2><h3>Extrinsic correction — measurement availability</h3><div class="panel">{{ validity_table(section.extrinsic) }}</div>
{% if section.timing %}<h3>Timing stress</h3><p class="note">Identity-only timing stress is separate from correction and pose recovery. An unmet timing request is unavailable evidence, never a successful zero error.</p><div class="panel">{{ validity_table(section.timing) }}</div>{% endif %}
<h3>Ground-contact baseline by GT range</h3><p class="note">These bins describe the yaw-zero reference. The oracle-controlled projection fixes the GT contact pixel; reconstruction uses a horizontal flat-plane model. Absolute residual can include a plane-model baseline even without a calibration fault. Missing measurements have no estimate.</p><div class="panel"><table><thead><tr><th>GT range / metres</th><th>Total objects</th><th>Measured</th><th>Invalid</th><th>Mean residual / metres</th><th>Reasons</th></tr></thead><tbody>{% for group in section.ranges %}<tr><td>{{ group.name }}</td><td>{{ number(group.total) }}</td><td>{{ number(group.count) }}</td><td>{{ number(group.invalid) }}</td><td>{% if group.mean %}{{ number(group.mean) }}{% else %}Unavailable{% endif %}</td><td>{% for reason in group.reasons %}{{ reason.text }} {{ number(reason.count) }}{% else %}None{% endfor %}</td></tr>{% endfor %}</tbody></table></div></section>{% endfor %}
<footer>Descriptive operator summaries. Formal statistical results require their separate approved artifacts and claims. Private scene rows, dataset files and checkpoints are not included in this report.</footer>
</main></body></html>
